  bounded row-count calculation used for resize. Empty/zero-height rows and
  maximum requested heights cannot stall startup or wrap the row accumulator.
- Restore XmSTRING_TAG_STRLEN (-1) in tag-cache input validation. Rejecting this
  documented sentinel prevented fresh-cache font-tag initialization and left
  most default-font labels blank. Add a native fresh-cache tag/label regression.
- Track both UIL source files when regenerating periodic.uid.
- Add native integration coverage of the real Periodic/UIL startup, seven
  appearance/resource cases, invalid options, missing UID data, RowColumn
  warnings and List geometry boundaries. Full visual redesign remains ongoing.

Separate appearance defaults from application resources (2026-10-26)
==================================================================

- Keep profile patterns outside the application Xrm database. Establish normal
  class/application resources before applying toolkit-owned modern defaults,
  so broad application wildcards retain precedence over class-specific styling.
- Preserve resource entries added after profile selection during live changes.
- Capture unstyled baselines for modern-created controls, including inherited
  parent colors in cached gadgets, so classic restoration uses classic values.
- Use Xt's cached pixel conversion in the widget's actual colormap rather than
  allocating appearance colors in the default screen colormap.
- Expand native parity to thirteen widget/gadget classes and nine cases covering
  all three profiles, broad overrides, modern-to-classic restoration, later
  resource edits and private 8-bit colormaps. Retain density, state, ownership,
  reentrancy, rollback and palette regressions.

