============================================================

- Extend the installed live-appearance consumer with real `XmText` and
  `XmTextField` widgets. Their committed values now remain intact through all
  profile transitions, covering the deferred output-backend initialization
  boundary used by the Motif bug fix.

Source-side drag teardown contract (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Add a source-contract regression requiring drag-finish atom release through
  the live source shell and direct retained-source lookup, guarding the
  owner-replacement lifetime fix alongside the installed DnD probes.

XLibre live property fixture (2026-10-25)
==========================================

- Add an opt-in installed consumer that mutates a writable XLibre output
  `DPI` property, waits for the coalesced shell observer transaction, verifies
  shell/descendant scale and callback output identity, and restores the
  original property on every exit path. Without a supplied XLibre display it
  explicitly returns the ordinary-Xvfb skip status; no fallback run is counted
  as live qualification.
- Add a source-contract regression for the live fixture's property restoration,
  teardown ordering, callback cardinality and real-display/status-77 boundary.
- Record live-fixture source and installed-`libXm` fingerprints, exact compile/
  run commands, elapsed time and the qualification result in `receipt.json`.
- Classify the receipt result explicitly as `pass`, `skip` or `fail`, keeping a
  successful ordinary-Xvfb rejection distinct from real-display qualification.

XLibre contract receipt provenance (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Extend `run-xlibre-dpi-contract.py` to write a durable `receipt.json` with
  source hashes, display mode, exact compile/run commands, elapsed time and
  installed `libXm` fingerprint. This keeps ordinary-Xvfb fallback evidence
  distinct from future real-XLibre qualification.

Display-scale transaction reentrancy guard (2026-10-25)
=========================================================

- Reject nested `XmSetDisplayScaleOverride`/display-scale transactions from
  a scale callback, preserving the outer override as authoritative. The
  installed fixture verifies callback invocation, nested rejection and
  cleanup; per-display transaction state is retired with the Motif display.

XLibre transient-query fallback (2026-10-25)
==============================================

- Return to the global display scale when a realized shell's client-area or
  RandR resource query is temporarily unavailable, instead of retaining a
  stale per-output scale. The source-contract regression covers initialization
  and each early-return fallback; real output hotplug qualification remains a
  separate XLibre gate.

XLibre vendor predicate hardening (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Require the server vendor string to be exactly `XLibre` or `XLibre` followed
  by whitespace and a version suffix. Substrings such as `NotXLibre` and
  `XLibre-server` are no longer treated as the versioned XLibre contract; the
  installed fixture covers positive, spoofed and malformed vendor names.

XLibre RandR property decode hardening (2026-10-25)
====================================================

- Validate the RandR property type, format, item count and trailing-byte
  metadata before reading the returned format-32 buffer. Malformed format-8
  or format-16 properties are now rejected without an out-of-bounds read;
  the installed contract fixture exercises the decode boundary under the
  sanitizer configuration.

Deterministic display-scale override (2026-10-25)
=================================================

- Add the `XmSetDisplayScaleOverride`, `XmGetDisplayScaleOverride` and
  `XmClearDisplayScaleOverride` API for deterministic per-display DPI
  simulation.  The installed consumer verifies invalid-input rejection,
  resource-database identity, live default-indicator reflow, toggle-state and
  explicit-resource preservation, and reversible cleanup.  The override now
  feeds the shared UI-thread transaction boundary used by the Xft/XLibre
  default path; complete historical-widget coverage remains open.  See
  `docs/display-scale-override.md`.
- Reflow toolkit-owned SpinBox arrow defaults when the live display scale
  changes, while preserving explicit `XmNarrowSize` values (including values
  supplied after construction). The installed display-scale fixture now
  covers reversible default reflow and explicit-size preservation.
- Extend the same live transaction to `XmProgressRing`'s toolkit-owned
  preferred dimensions and scale-derived stroke repaint, while preserving
  explicit width and height resources.
- Qualify the 96/144/192/288-DPI gallery scale matrix across ToggleButton,
  SpinBox and ProgressRing. Correct ProgressRing's inherited Primitive
  geometry bookkeeping so parent negotiation cannot make a toolkit default
  look application-owned during a later live scale transition.
- Update the `--enable-unicode-text` configure probe to use `atomic_init`,
  which remains available when current GCC and Clang drivers select C23 mode.

ScrolledWindow display-scale defaults (2026-10-25)
===================================================

- Scale automatic `XmScrolledWindow` toolkit-owned 100-pixel width and height
