- Let command error history updates call the public list APIs without an
  outer application lock.

Guard text-field selection extraction allocations (2026-10-26)
===============================================================

- Reject reversed or unrepresentable selection ranges and handle allocation
  failure before copying narrow or wide selection data; clamp conversion
  output before adding the terminator.

Guard text-field string getter allocations (2026-10-26)
========================================================

- Check multibyte and wide-string allocation sizes and allocator results, and
  explicitly terminate successful conversion output.
- Handle allocation failure for the empty wide-string result as well.

Guard wide text-field modify-verify allocation (2026-10-26)
============================================================

- Bound the temporary wide-character buffer, check allocation failure, and
  avoid narrowing an unsuccessful or oversized `mbstowcs` result to `int`.
- Apply equivalent bounds and cleanup to the callback-converted multibyte
  buffer.

Reject oversized text-field setter lengths (2026-10-26)
========================================================

- Reject narrow and multibyte input lengths that cannot fit the callback
  `int` length before changing widget state.

Preserve text-field conversion result widths (2026-10-26)
==========================================================

- Keep `wcstombs` and `mbstowcs` result counts in `size_t` throughout public
  getter and substring conversion paths instead of narrowing them to `int`.
- Apply the same width to the wide-string setter conversion result.
- Check its temporary conversion allocation before passing it to `wcstombs`.

Bound text-field substring position narrowing (2026-10-26)
============================================================

- Saturate source ranges beyond the public `int` count at `INT_MAX` and
  return `XmCOPY_TRUNCATED` instead of wrapping a large `XmTextPosition`.

Saturate text-field multibyte byte counting (2026-10-26)
=========================================================

- Prevent the wide-character byte-count helper from wrapping its `int`
  accumulator when calculating substring sizes.
Guard MWM frame-part geometry inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------
GetFramePartInfo now rejects a null client record or missing output pointers
before reading decoration state or writing geometry.  Existing valid callers
retain the same frame-part calculations while malformed requests fail safely.

Guard MWM frame-part hit-test inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------
IdentifyFramePart now returns FRAME_NONE for a null client record before
reading frame state.  Normal event hit testing is unchanged.

Guard MWM frame/client conversion inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------
FrameToClient and ClientToFrame now leave their arguments unchanged when the
client record or any conversion pointer is null.  Valid coordinate conversion
behavior is unchanged.

Guard MWM depressed-gadget geometry inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------------
GetDepressInfo now rejects a null client record or missing geometry output
pointer before reading decoration state or computing bevel dimensions.

Guard MWM gadget hit-test arrays (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------------------
GadgetID now returns FRAME_NONE for a null gadget array instead of
dereferencing it when a nonzero count is supplied.

Guard MWM system-menu placement inputs (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------------------------
GetSystemMenuPosition now leaves its outputs unchanged when the client record
or either output coordinate pointer is null.  Valid placement behavior is
unchanged.

Guard MWM gadget-state inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------
PushGadgetIn and PopGadgetOut now no-op for null client records before
changing decoration flags or regenerating frame display lists.

Guard MWM title-text rectangle inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------
GetTextBox now returns without writing when its client record or output
rectangle is null.

Guard MWM frame exposure inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------
FrameWindow now returns `FALSE`, while FrameExposureProc and BaseWinExposureProc
no-op, when passed a null client record before touching frame windows or GCs.

Guard MWM frame regeneration inputs (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------------
RegenerateClientFrame now no-op for a null client record before reading
decoration state or resizing frame subwindows.

Guard MWM frame construction inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------
ConstructFrame and GenerateFrameDisplayLists now reject null client records
before reading decoration or geometry state, preventing malformed lifecycle
callbacks from dereferencing invalid frame data.

Guard MWM client adoption inputs (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------
AdoptClient now ignores a null client record before touching save-set,
geometry, or reparenting state.

Validate MWM stretcher geometry before window creation (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
CreateStretcherWindows now honors GetFramePartInfo failure and skips a
stretcher instead of passing uninitialized coordinates or dimensions to the X
server.

Guard MWM frame shape inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------
SetFrameShape now ignores a null client record before reading border, matte,
or shaped-window state.

Guard MWM decoration allocation inputs (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------------
CountFrameRectangles and InitClientDecoration now ignore null screen records,
and AllocateFrameDisplayLists returns `FALSE` for a null client record before
reading appearance or decoration state.

Guard MWM title drawing inputs (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------
DrawWindowTitle now returns before reading decoration state when called with a
null client record.

Handle MWM gadget bevel allocation failure (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------------
DepressGadget now retries missing static bevel lists and returns `FALSE` until
both allocations succeed, avoiding unconditional dereferences after a partial
allocation failure.

Guard compact MWM maximize geometry (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------
BevelMaximizeButton now skips heights below five pixels before unsigned
subtraction can wrap its icon dimensions.

Guard compact MWM system/minimize geometry (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------------
BevelSystemButton and BevelMinimizeButton now reject undersized heights before
their unsigned geometry calculations, avoiding wrapped dimensions in compact
title bars.

Guard narrow MWM system-button geometry (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------------
BevelSystemButton now rejects widths below the minimum required by each glyph
size branch before subtracting from the unsigned width.

Validate MWM bevel primitive geometry (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------
BevelRectangle and BevelDepressedRectangle now reject null lists, empty boxes,
overflowing bevel-width sums, bevels wider than their boxes, and invalid
inset widths before generating shadow rectangles.

Guard MWM stretcher-corner dimensions (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------------------------
StretcherCorner now rejects missing lists, undersized corners, and border
widths wider than the corner before computing unsigned offsets and extents.

Guard MWM text drawing inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------
DrawStringInBox and WmDrawString now return for missing display, graphics,
font, box, string, or active-screen inputs before calling Xlib text routines.

Guard MWM compound-string drawing inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------
WmDrawXmString now returns for missing display, font list, compound string,
graphics, clip box, or active-screen inputs before measuring or drawing text.

Guard MWM icon screen fallback (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------
MakeIconPixmap now returns `None` when neither the client nor the active MWM
screen supplies a screen record, avoiding a null-screen dereference during
startup or teardown.

Bound MWM cached-label bitmap lookup (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------
MakeCachedLabelPixmap now rejects missing screen/widget inputs and indices
outside the populated bitmap cache before indexing the cache array.

Guard MWM named-icon fallback inputs (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------------
MakeNamedIconPixmap now rejects a null client record and only attempts named
pixmap lookup when the client has a screen record; otherwise it safely uses the
existing default-icon path.

Complete MWM named-icon screen fallback (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------------
MakeNamedIconPixmap now selects the client screen or active screen once and
uses that record for the built-in fallback, avoiding a second null-screen
dereference when named lookup is skipped.

Guard inconsistent MWM bitmap-cache metadata (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------------------
GetBitmapIndex now rejects a nonzero bitmap-cache count with a null cache
pointer before iterating cache entries.

Recover MWM bitmap-cache allocation retries (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------------------------------
GetBitmapIndex now clears stale nonzero cache-size metadata when an empty cache
has a null allocation, allowing later lookups to retry the initial allocation
after a transient memory failure.

Handle MWM icon X resource failure (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------
MakeIconPixmap now returns `None` when pixmap or graphics-context creation
fails, freeing a partially created icon pixmap before returning.

Validate MWM cached-label bitmap entries (2026-10-26)
