Own TabBox font tables and mutable drawing contexts (2026-10-26)
================================================================

- Retain the copied render-table handle on fontList/renderTable updates instead
  of discarding it through an accidental comparison. Caller-owned tables can
  be freed after SetValues; default restoration and widget teardown remain
  valid.
- Use a private drawing GC, update it in place during redisplay and free it once
  at destruction. Mutable tab drawing no longer changes a shared Xt GC or uses
  a stale local handle after a theme change.
- Extend the native realized-widget regression with repeated font-alias updates,
  caller release, measured text extents and default restoration.

Guard MWM frame-window construction failures (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------------------
ConstructFrame now checks each X window allocation before creating children or
mapping the hierarchy, and tears down partial frame windows on failure. This
prevents invalid-parent and invalid-window requests after X resource exhaustion.

Guard MWM active icon-label window allocation (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------------
CreateActiveIconTextWindow now handles an XCreateWindow failure explicitly,
leaving the optional active label disabled instead of recording an invalid
parent and allowing later label operations to target a missing window.

Guard MWM icon-frame window allocation (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------------
MakeIcon now rejects an icon whose frame-window allocation returned `None`,
avoiding subsequent shadow, reparent, and event operations against an invalid
window resource.

Guard MWM active icon-label hide/move paths (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------------------
HideActiveIconText now resolves one validated label window before deleting its
context or unmapping it, and MoveActiveIconText validates its client and
screen state. Failed optional label creation therefore cannot cause a
BadWindow request during cleanup or repositioning.

Guard MWM active icon-label show inputs (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------
ShowActiveIconText now validates the client, screen, active label window, and
icon frame before querying attributes or changing the label. Failed or
partially torn-down icons therefore return cleanly without invalid X requests.

Guard MWM client icon reparenting (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------
ReparentIconWindow now validates both window IDs and the XGetGeometry status
before changing geometry or reparenting a client-provided icon. An icon that
was destroyed by its owner no longer leaves uninitialized geometry in MWM.

Handle MWM active icon geometry-query failures (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------------------------
ShowActiveIconText and MoveActiveIconText now stop when querying the icon
frame geometry fails, avoiding placement calculations from uninitialized
coordinates after an icon owner destroys or reparents the frame.

Handle MWM active icon attribute-query failures (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------------------------
ShowActiveIconText now requires XGetWindowAttributes to succeed before using
the icon frame's event mask. A frame that disappears during activation no
longer leaves an uninitialized mask for XChangeWindowAttributes.

Handle MWM confirmation-window geometry failure (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------------------------------------
GetWmClientInfo now checks XGetGeometry for confirmation windows before
copying dimensions into client state. If the managed window disappears during
initialization, MWM aborts that client setup instead of using uninitialized
size and border values.

Make MWM frame teardown safe for partial construction (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
FreeClientFrame now accepts a null client pointer and only destroys a realized
frame window. Failed ConstructFrame paths can therefore be cleaned up
idempotently without dereferencing absent state or sending XDestroyWindow for
`None`.

Make MWM icon teardown safe with absent workspace storage (2026-10-26)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
FreeIcon now checks the WSM workspace list before reading its first icon
frame, and both WSM and non-WSM paths destroy only realized icon windows.
Partial icon setup and repeated teardown no longer dereference missing state
or issue XDestroyWindow for `None`.

Guard MWM dialog frame map/unmap operations (2026-10-26)
----------------------------------------------------------
WithdrawDialog and ReManageDialog now map or unmap a client frame only when
the frame window exists. Dialog lifecycle callbacks after partial construction
therefore avoid invalid X requests while preserving normal behavior.

Guard MWM unmanage frame withdrawal (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------------------------
UnManageWindow now checks that a normal or maximized client has a realized
frame before unmapping it. Clients that fail during frame construction can be
withdrawn without issuing an X request for `None`.

Skip destroyed MWM embedded clients during shutdown (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------------------
UnParentControls now excludes embedded clients already marked destroyed
before removing them from save sets or reparenting/unmapping their windows.
This avoids stale X requests during front-panel shutdown.

Clear MWM child frame IDs after teardown (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------------------------
FreeClientFrame now clears the cached title and base child IDs together with
the destroyed frame ID. Later repaint, cleanup, or remanage paths cannot reuse
child XIDs that were removed when the parent frame was destroyed.

